<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ariarathes I of Cappadocia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 322 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ariarathes I was the Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> of Cappadocia who kept control of the region after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>. In 322 BCE the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perdiccas">Perdiccas</a> invaded Cappadocia to install Eumenes, defeated Ariarathes and had him executed. His adopted son Ariarathes II later regained the land, and his line became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariarathid-dynasty">Ariarathid dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ariarathes-i-of-cappadocia.jpg" alt="Ariarathes I of Cappadocia" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:LouisAragon (uploader) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Ariarathes_I_of_Cappadocia,_minted_in_Gaziura.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
